# Line endings. Every tracked text file is already stored LF in the index
# (verified: `git ls-files --eol` shows i/lf for all 83), and this pins that
# contract so a differently-configured clone can't start committing CRLF.
# eol= is deliberately NOT set: this repo's Windows checkouts run with
# core.autocrlf=true and rewriting every working copy to LF would be pure
# churn. To stop the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" notices locally, set
# core.autocrlf=input rather than adding eol= here.
* text=auto

# Binary — never diff, never line-ending-convert. Source spreadsheets are
# gitignored (see .gitignore) but a force-added one must not be mangled.
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
